        <p>Quiet Resilience — Builds the inner steadiness that allows recovery from emotional and energetic depletion</p>
        <p>Inner Alignment — Encourages a return to one's own centre — more balanced, more grounded, more clear</p>
        <p>Colour-Based Guidance</p>
        <p>Tourmaline is one of the few gemstones where colour meaningfully shapes the experience — and where the choice of colour can guide toward a specific quality of support.</p>
        <p>Green Tourmaline carries a softer, more accessible energy than Emerald — chosen when Mercury's qualities of clarity and calm thinking are needed without the full intensity of a primary planetary stone.</p>
        <p>Red Tourmaline (Rubellite) offers a more tolerant alternative to Ruby — warmth, vitality, and quiet confidence without the force that a Sun stone carries.</p>
        <p>Blue Tourmaline (Indicolite) is rare, thoughtful, and quietly intense — chosen for depth, truthful expression, and the kind of inward clarity that contemplative temperaments seek.</p>
        <p>Bi-colour / Watermelon Tourmaline is chosen for its unique quality of holding contrast in harmony — the meeting of opposites within a single stone, prized for individuality as much as beauty.</p>
        <p>In all cases: chosen when balance and tolerance matter more than intensity.</p>
